    "time": "14:44:29 UTC",
    "body": "Good. Full write-up of the clamp rationale, since three people asked: clamping after the hop keeps single-channel grayscale tensors from clipping at the low end, which is what was washing out the darks. Before the hop it also interacts badly with the normalized multipliers, pushing mid-tones up by almost a tenth. The kernel now does hop, clamp, blend, in that order, and the schematic Priya posted matches this sequence exactly."
  },
